data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/final-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclaude — final report\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three criteria satisfied and independently verified.\\n\\n## What happened\\n1. Dispatched the full task (d002) to teammate `dev` in one shot, since the\\n   mission is small and all-or-nothing.\\n2. `dev` implemented `src/greet.py` (`greet(name)` -\u003e `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`) and\\n   `tests/test_greet.py` (two unittest cases: normal name, empty string),\\n   committed to its own branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`,\\n   commit `67f067d`), and reported success with test output.\\n3. Judged independently rather than trusting the report: fetched `dev`'s\\n   branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev subject`, confirmed real tree\\n   changes vs. base), inspected both files directly via `git show`, and\\n   re-ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself in a fresh git\\n   worktree checked out at `dev`'s commit. Got the same result: exit code 0,\\n   2 tests passed.\\n4. Accepted `dev`'s work (`cs-campaign-member accept dev`).\\n5. Fast-forward merged `dev`'s commit onto my own branch\\n   (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) at commit\\n   `67f067d`, and re-ran the test command there too — same clean pass — so\\n   the verified deliverable is committed on my branch, not only dev's.\\n\\n## Verification evidence\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\nEXIT: 0\\n```\\n\\n`src/greet.py`:\\n```python\\ndef greet(name):\\n    return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"\\n```\\n\\n`tests/test_greet.py`: two cases, `test_normal_name` (`greet(\\\"World\\\") ==\\n\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string` (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\nNo unmet criteria; no open issues.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

